### Peticiones de auth (REST Client de VS Code o compatible)
### Requiere auth en http://localhost:8080. Usuarios de prueba del laboratorio.

@authUrl = http://localhost:8080

### Salud del servicio
GET {{authUrl}}/q/health

### Login válido (student) -> 200 con token JWT, expiresIn y user
# @name loginStudent
POST {{authUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "student",
  "password": "Workshop123!",
  "client": "angular-workshop"
}

### Login válido (trainer) -> 200
POST {{authUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "trainer",
  "password": "Trainer123!"
}

### Password incorrecta -> 401 { "message": "Invalid username or password" }
POST {{authUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "student",
  "password": "incorrecta"
}

### Usuario inexistente -> 401 (mismo mensaje genérico)
POST {{authUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "nadie",
  "password": "Workshop123!"
}

### Sin username -> 400 { "message": "Username is required" }
POST {{authUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "password": "Workshop123!"
}

### Sin password -> 400 { "message": "Password is required" }
POST {{authUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "student"
}

### CORS: origen permitido (http://localhost:4200) -> Access-Control-Allow-Origin
OPTIONS {{authUrl}}/auth/login
Origin: http://localhost:4200
Access-Control-Request-Method: POST

### CORS: origen no permitido -> 403 (Quarkus rechaza el origen)
OPTIONS {{authUrl}}/auth/login
Origin: http://sitio-no-permitido.example
Access-Control-Request-Method: POST
